unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]

input bank: observed

input rent_amt: money PLN

input rent_day: date

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

place unexplained: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move rent[f in flats]: transfers
  on rent_day
  when pos(f) == 2 or pos(f) == 3 or pos(f) == 11
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

ask led: residuals konto 2026-02

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 2 000.00 PLN
  rent_day = 2026-02-03
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version statement_02
  cite bank_feed
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-03-02
  covers konto
  pad konto from unexplained
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to landlord amount 2 000.00 PLN, fulfils: rent[f11]) "line 1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-02-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to landlord amount 2 000.00 PLN, fulfils: rent[f3]) "line 2"
  bank[r3] = (on: 2026-02-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to landlord amount 2 000.00 PLN, fulfils: rent[f2]) "line 3"
  stated[konto] = 4 000.00 PLN at 2026-02-28 end "saldo"
,,1:0,664:led: residuals konto 2026-02
  2026-02 balance: model 4 000.00 PLN, observed 4 000.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN
    balance konto 2026-02-28 end (padded): booked 4 000.00 PLN, stated 4 000.00 PLN, gap 0.00 PLN
  2026-02 move rent: model -6 000.00 PLN, observed -6 000.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN
    matched rent[f2] on 2026-02-03: model -2 000.00 PLN, observed -2 000.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN, timing +0 days
    matched rent[f3] on 2026-02-03: model -2 000.00 PLN, observed -2 000.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN, timing +0 days
    matched rent[f11] on 2026-02-03: model -2 000.00 PLN, observed -2 000.00 PLN, difference 0.00 PLN, timing +0 days
  cut 2026-10-20
,15:g12/order_typed,3:g12,25:run g12/order_typed.tally,1498:21:g12/order_typed.tally,1467:model g12_order_typed
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #39), G12: L §2.5 binding order, E §4.1: a binding over movements runs in the movement order, by day, then that order's other terms, each compared as its own type. zfee, a day earlier, comes first whatever its id; then rent[f2], rent[f3] and rent[f11], keys of a list index in index order. The twin pair rent[f2] and rent[f3] sorts the same as text; tally 2.1.1 compared the order's text and put rent[f11] between rent[f2] and rent[f3]. Strata of 10 or more are not here: S builds no binding over decisions (M1)."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]

input rent_amt: money PLN

input fee_amt: money PLN

input rent_day: date

input fee_day: date

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move rent[f in flats]: transfers
  on rent_day
  when pos(f) == 2 or pos(f) == 3 or pos(f) == 11
  leg cash from konto to world amount rent_amt

move zfee: transfers
  on fee_day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee_amt

ask q_keys: m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-02

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 10.00 PLN
  fee_amt = 1.00 PLN
  rent_day = 2026-02-03
  fee_day = 2026-02-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
,,1:0,289:q_keys (m = zfee): 1.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: zfee
  cut 2026-06-30
q_keys (m = rent[f2]): 10.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f2]
  cut 2026-06-30
q_keys (m = rent[f3]): 10.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f3]
  cut 2026-06-30
q_keys (m = rent[f11]): 10.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f11]
  cut 2026-06-30
,13:g6/currencies,2:g6,23:run g6/currencies.tally,1725:19:g6/currencies.tally,1696:model g6_currencies
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #43), G6: L §5.4, §5.7, §5.14: a declared currency is a key of the prelude's currencies, so a leg of unit kind currencies carries money in any declared currency: in_pln moves 25.00 PLN into konto and in_eur 7.00 EUR into konto_eur. The twin in_fixed carries PLN on a leg of a kind whose unit is PLN itself. tally 2.1.1's refcore refused the load (LOAD-UNIT the amount of leg cash of in_eur is money EUR, not a unit of currencies), though its run took it."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind curs: event certain
  leg cash: currencies

kind plns: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

input pln_amt: money PLN

input eur_amt: money EUR

input day: date

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place konto_eur: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move in_pln: curs
  on day
  at day
  leg cash from world to konto amount pln_amt

move in_eur: curs
  on day
  at day
  leg cash from world to konto_eur amount eur_amt

move in_fixed: plns
  on day
  at day
  leg cash from world to konto amount pln_amt

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto_eur, 2026-03-31)

ask f: flows(in_pln, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31), flows(in_eur, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31), flows(in_fixed, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pln_amt = 25.00 PLN
  eur_amt = 7.00 EUR
  day = 2026-02-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto_eur] = 0 EUR at 2026-01-01 start
,,1:0,244:f: (25.00 PLN, 7.00 EUR, 25.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: in_eur
  unfulfilled: in_fixed
  unfulfilled: in_pln
  cut 2026-06-30
q: (100.00 PLN, 150.00 PLN, 7.00 EUR)
  unfulfilled: in_eur
  unfulfilled: in_fixed
  unfulfilled: in_pln
  cut 2026-06-30
,16:g11/settle_order,3:g11,26:run g11/settle_order.tally,2171:22:g11/settle_order.tally,2139:model g11_settle_order
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #44), G11: L §5.14.3 How a settlement leg counts, E §5 step 5, E §3.2: turn swaps t[2026-03]'s places, so bank[r1], settling its adjustment, is refused (RUN-RECORD, the leg is turned round), and linking is all or nothing: every read that counts the adjustment meets that refusal, in either order, two reads in one ask (q_fb: flows then a balance; q_bf: the balance then flows; q_ff: flows twice). The twin g11/settle_order_twin moves only the leg's from place, and its row settles: both orders answer the same numbers. tally 2.1.1's refcore linked the adjustment before the refusal, so the later read of an ask took the HOLE-CHANGED hole, and swapping the reads swapped the answers."

